The final solution requires modifications to two files.

**1. `ChatRipple-C//config.h`**
A new line should be added:
```c
// Add this line, for example, after the other #defines for features.
#define ENABLE_URL_STRIPPING 1
```

**2. `ChatRipple-C//src//pipeline//preprocessor.c`**
This file needs two changes: the new function and the modification to `preprocess_text`.

*New Function `strip_urls` (Example Implementation):*
```c
#include <string.h>

// A new function to strip URLs in-place.
void strip_urls(char *text) {
    char *current_pos = text;
    while ((current_pos = strstr(current_pos, "http")) != NULL) {
        char *end_pos = strpbrk(current_pos, " \t\n\r"); // Find the end of the URL
        if (end_pos == NULL) { // URL is at the end of the string
            *current_pos = '\0';
            break;
        } else {
            // Overwrite the URL by moving the rest of the string forward
            memmove(current_pos, end_pos, strlen(end_pos) + 1);
        }
    }
}
```

*Modified `preprocess_text` function:*
```c
// Inside the existing preprocess_text function
void preprocess_text(char *raw_text) {
    // ... (existing preprocessing steps like to_lowercase, remove_punctuation)

    // Conditionally call the new URL stripping function
    #ifdef ENABLE_URL_STRIPPING
        strip_urls(raw_text);
    #endif

    // ... (rest of the function, e.g., tokenization)
}
```
